            <ArticleTitle>Side balloon stenting of the left main bifurcation: a three-year angiographic follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>547-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8183.2009.00502.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>None of the currently used interventional techniques yield durable results for coronary bifurcation lesions. We successfully treated a patient with unprotected left main bifurcation disease using a side balloon stent technique with a drug-eluting stent (DES). This technique produced excellent immediate and long-term results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
